From 121af7cb4050da1f673ea4f2a8c7a9b175f209ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jsfpechar-ops <jsf.pechar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:45:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Stop treating late filings as failures and stop resending
 refused records

The Foreign Police answered the open UbyPort questions in writing
(CPR-34587-2/CJ-2026-930023): the outcome depends only on each code's
severity, 112 means reported late and is an accept, and resending refused
records counts against the host. Our earlier reading of 112 as 'batch not
received' kept accepted guests in the queue and risked duplicates.

Also lets the mock behave like the police test environment and accepts the
six-character abbreviation the police issued for the WS test account.
